# ============================================================================
# Triage 2026-09-23 — the unbound 1.26.0 DNSSEC-validator advisory (#1668 dev /
# #1669 main). A feed event, not a closure change: the 2026-09-22 nightly (run
# 35711419780) was green on BOTH lanes against the same closures this run
# scans — the 2026-09-21 pin advance (#1662) had already merged and been
# scanned green — and the findings delta across the two runs is 1 added,
# 0 removed, against exactly ONE package on each ref. No exception expired
# either (the next grid date is 2026-09-30), so nothing in this repo caused it.
#
# Real product match, no CPE collision: NLnet Labs unbound, CVE-2026-81642
# (NVD 9.8 CRITICAL, CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H). A DNSKEY
# whose owner name is a compression pointer into its own RDATA overflows the
# digest buffer in the DNSSEC validator — denial of service and possibly RCE
# through attacker-controlled data. Affects "up to and including 1.26.0";
# fixed upstream in 1.26.1 (2026-09-16).
#
# Provenance RE-VERIFIED 2026-09-23 against the built closure rather than
# carried over from the 2026-07-26 unbound block's note. `nix why-depends` on
# the runtime closure of `.#devkitImageEnv`:
#
#   devcontainer-image-env -> podman 5.8.6 -> gpgme 2.0.1 -> gnupg 2.4.9
#     -> gnutls 3.8.13 -> unbound-1.26.0-lib
#
# Only the `lib` output is present: `nix path-info -r` reports
# unbound-1.26.0-lib and nothing else, and the env exposes no unbound
# executable at all. The sole consumer is libgnutls-dane.so — the only gnutls
# library that references libunbound — i.e. DANE certificate verification.
#
# Reachability: the advisory's vector is an unbound RESOLVER digesting DNSKEYs
# from a zone the attacker controls. This image ships no resolver — no daemon,
# no unbound binary, no service — so the vulnerable path is reached only if
# something calls gnutls' DANE API, which nothing in the closure does by
# default. Same shape as the 2026-07-26 unbound 1.25.1 block, with the
# provenance verified this time rather than asserted.
#
# Remediation lever: exists, but has nowhere to land today. nixos-26.05,
# staging-26.05 and master ALL still ship 1.26.0 with no CVE-named patch. The
# bump (NixOS/nixpkgs#564725) merged to `staging` on 2026-09-22 and the
# staging-26.05 backport (NixOS/nixpkgs#565869) opened the same day and is
# still open, so the fix is two branch hops from the pinned channel. 2026-11-04
# gives it six weeks and keeps this block on its own Wednesday; it dies on the
# advance that ships unbound 1.26.1 and should be DELETED then, not renewed.
